# The names systemdict holds that PLRM 8.2 does not define.
#
# This is the enumeration of the non-standard language surface: every name
# a program reaches in one token that the specification does not describe.
# It is a LIST rather than a count, because a count is a property of the
# build and not of the language. The device loaders depend on which devices
# were compiled in, NOFACES on whether a face library was found, WIN32 on
# the platform -- so a count is a different number on every configuration,
# and a register holding one reports a Windows build, a faceless build and
# a macOS build as each having a name the others do not. MEASURED: it went
# red on the faceless lane for NOFACES and on macOS for the device loaders.
#
# A name's ABSENCE therefore never fails. Its ARRIVAL always does: a name
# here is one somebody wrote down and said why, and a name in systemdict
# that is in neither this list nor PLRM 8.2 is a surface nobody declared.
#
# Each entry says what a program may do with the name. That is the part
# worth reviewing: an operator that only answers is a different thing from
# one that runs a procedure the program supplied, and a name that is inert
# in a shipped run is different again.

# --- the page sizes (PLRM Appendix; a program calls them to set a size)
11x17
a3
a4
a4small
a5
b4
b5
ledger
legal
letter
lettersmall
note

# --- separation and custom colour (Adobe separation convention). Each
# --- takes program data and answers; none runs a program's procedure.
customcolorimage
findcmykcustomcolor
findrgbcustomcolor
separationimage
setcustomcolor

# --- Level 3 colour and raster extensions: parameter pairs, get and set
currentoverprintmode
setoverprintmode
currentrasteropcode
setrasteropcode

# --- distiller parameters and pdfmark: parameter dictionaries and an
# --- annotation the vector writers read. Program data in, no callback.
currentdistillerparams
setdistillerparams
pdfmark

# --- printing shorthands, and the string = uses
=only
==only
=print
=string

# --- the error names PLRM 3.11 defines outside the 8.2 operator list.
# --- $error is writable BY DESIGN: it is where a program reads what went
# --- wrong, and errordict handlers write it.
$error
handleerror
signalerror

# --- the environment pair. REFUSED once the sandbox is engaged
# --- (xpost_path_control_is_engaged), so a shipped sandboxed run answers
# --- nothing through either; listed because what is held here is what a
# --- program can NAME, and a name that refuses today stops refusing if
# --- its guard moves.
getenv
putenv

# --- Display PostScript
flushpage

# --- the embedding interface: hands control back to the caller, which
# --- ends the run where it stands, as PLRM's own quit does
returntocaller

# --- the device loaders. Which of these exist depends on what was
# --- compiled in, which is why absence must not fail. Each loads a
# --- driver written in this tree, not one a program supplies.
loadbgrdevice
loadjpegdevice
loadpngalphadevice
loadpngdevice
loadrasterdevice
loadrecorddevice
loadxcbdevice

# --- facts about the build, put here by the C so a program can know what
# --- it may ask for before it asks. Booleans; a program reads them.
NOFACES
WIN32
